spans.s:
cl. 1. Ā. (Dhātup. xii, 6) प॑णते (ep. also ˚ति; pf. पेणे Gr.; aor. अपणिष्ट, Bhaṭṭ.; fut. पणिष्यते, ˚णिता, ib.),
to honour, praise, Naigh. iii, 14;
to barter, purchase, buy, Br.; MBh.;
to negotiate, bargain, Āpast.;
to bet, stake, lay a wager, play for (with gen. [e.g. प्राणा-नाम्, Bhaṭṭ.; cf. Pāṇ. ii, 3, 57., Kāś.] or acc. [e.g. कृष्णां] MBh.);
to risk or hazard (as a battle), MBh.;
to win anything (instr.) from (acc.), ib. :
Caus. पणयति (aor. अपीपणत्), to negotiate, bargain, Kāv. (cf. पणाय and √ पन्.)

(prob. invented to serve as the root of the words below) cl. 1. Ā. पण्डते, to go, move, Dhātup. viii, 29;
 cl. 10. P. पण्डयति, to heap together, pile up (v.l. for पिण्ड्), xxxii, 130; Vop.;
 cl. 1. or cl. 10. P. पण्डति, ˚डयति, to destroy, annihilate, xxxii, 73 (v.l. for पंस्).
